    "note": "Enrolled version (82nd Session, 2023). Section 4 and 5 lead sentences are quoted only up to the colon; the exceptions that follow cross struck text and are not quoted. The bill strikes the old requirement tying the serial-number rule to federal law and repeals NRS 202.3645 (Section 9)."
  },
  "operative_text": "Section 1 (new section in NRS chapter 202): Except as otherwise provided in subsection 2, a person shall not possess or cause a firearm to be present in, or within 100 feet of the entrance of, a place the person knows or reasonably should know is an election site.\nSection 1 (new section in NRS chapter 202): A person shall not knowingly possess a firearm or cause a firearm to be present at an election site with the specific intent to disrupt, interfere with or monitor the administration of the election, the counting of votes or any person who is voting or attempting to vote.\nSection 1 (new section in NRS chapter 202): A person who violates subsection 1 is guilty of a gross misdemeanor.\nSection 1 (new section in NRS chapter 202): A person who violates subsection 3 is guilty of a category D felony and shall be punished as provided in NRS 193.130.\nSection 2 (NRS 202.253): “Market frame or receiver” means an object that is marketed or sold to the public to become or to be used as the frame or receiver of a firearm once completed, assembled or converted.\nSection 2 (NRS 202.253): “Ready frame or receiver” means any forging, casting, printing, extrusion, machined body or similar article that has reached a stage in manufacturing where it may readily be completed, assembled or converted to be used as the frame or receiver of a functional firearm.\nSection 4 (NRS 202.3625): A person shall not sell, offer to sell or transfer an unfinished frame or receiver , ready frame or receiver or market frame or receiver unless:\nSection 5 (NRS 202.363): A person shall not possess, purchase, transport or receive an unfinished frame or receiver , ready frame or receiver or market frame or receiver unless:\nSection 8: The amendatory provisions of this act do not apply to a person who possesses a ready frame or receiver or a market frame or receiver before October 1, 2023."
}